ion of novel RNA-based medicines for the treatment of genetic neurodevelopmental diseases. The company was formerly known as ASOthera Pharmaceuticals, Inc. and changed its name to Stoke Therapeutics, Inc. in May 2016. Stoke Therapeutics, Inc. was incorporated in 2014 and is headquartered in Bedford, Massachusetts.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Ian F. Smith A.C.A., C.P.A. | CEO & Director | Age 59 | Compensation: $1.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 170 people. Revenue per employee of $1.1M ranks in the top quartile among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 146%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $264K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $190K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Stoke Therapeutics, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $1.7B market cap on $184M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +146% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +276.7pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -661% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $45M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 24 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, thin -2287.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 17% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 3.6% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"s